Z||000000||fldevel||10-01-2000||11:27 AM|||| It all started about a week ago when my car was grinding into gears ..i have a 4 sp manual ..so i took it to the  shop and they did there BS to it and charged me $80 and now it sounds like the tranny is coming apart it sounds like sumthing is rattling or loose and hitting some gears in there sounds like a hard knocking grind like type noise .is this sumthing simple or am i loking at a new tranny ..all help is appreciated ||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||10-02-2000||01:53 PM||||Just what sort of $80 BS did they do?  Adjust linkage(s)?<P>"Grinding into gears" sounds like clutch not disengaging.   ||||reg||5
Z||000002||PJ||10-02-2000||09:51 PM||||Drain the fluid and look for metal. Check that the output seals aren't pushed out, damaged or leaking indicating that the carrier bearings are going. Sounds like the transaxle needs to come out if its not the clutch hydraulics.<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||stsmithgt||10-03-2000||09:43 AM||||Sorry to hear about your tranny.  It sounds like you've been to the same BS manufacturers as I have.  AS FOR NOW!  I just had my car picked up by the anti BSers, the Fiero Shop. (yeah) I can hardly wait to get it back.  Oh yeah, sorry if I'm bugging you like a pestering mut at your ankle asking when I get my car back.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Thanks George, and crew.    Todd<p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 10-03-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||fldevel||10-03-2000||06:52 PM||||ok .. i looked at my fiero service manual to figure out whare to add/check my tranny oil ...there wasent any in the damn trans axel so i added a quart or so of 10w30 and took it around the block and after a few minutes all the noise stopped ...i guess sometimes you just have to do things yourself to make shure its done properly ..||||reg||10
